{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And the silver of them that were numbered of the congregation.</b> Scripture explained to you what was done with the silver and the copper, because the silver served as the sockets, and upon the sockets the Tabernacle stood, and moreover many vessels were made from the silver and from the copper. But regarding the gold it did not explain, because no complete vessel was made from it — only the menorah and the cover — but things were overlaid with it, such as the planks, the ark, the inner altar, the table, and the poles." "<b>A hundred talents and a thousand and seven hundred and seventy-five.</b> They are twelve thousand and seventy-one mannah of secular weight, which are the weights called marcass."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:02:09.287358742Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}